Package: libqcomtee-dev
Architecture: arm64
Section: libdevel
Description: Qualcomm qcomtee userspace library
 QCOM-TEE (libqcomtee) is a user-space C library that enables applications
 to communicate with Qualcomm's Trusted Execution Environment (QTEE) via the
 Linux TEE subsystem using object-based IPC.
 .
 This package contains the static library libqcomtee.a and the development
 headers used to build applications against qcomtee.
Depends:
 libcbor-dev,
 ${misc:Depends},

Package: qcomtee-tests
Architecture: arm64
Description: Qualcomm qcomtee userspace library - test utility
 QCOM-TEE (libqcomtee) is a user-space C library that enables applications
 to communicate with Qualcomm's Trusted Execution Environment (QTEE) via the
 Linux TEE subsystem using object-based IPC.
 .
 This package contains the qcomteetest utility, which exercises libqcomtee
 against QTEE on the target device: it prints QTEE diagnostics and can load
 a test Trusted Application and invoke commands on it. It requires a QTEE
 capable device exposed through the Linux TEE subsystem.
 .
 The test Trusted Application is installed to /usr/lib/qcomtee-tests/. It is
 signed with Qualcomm test keys and can only be loaded on devices that accept
 test-signed images.
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
